{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779386156,"nonce":"Y7hIUUtUnOLsoKj8eYLKyZ/oTy0=","title":"Live execution: generic SSH, RunPod, Modal, logs, artifacts, manifests","message":"## Purpose\n\nConcrete live-execution child from `a3e46d5` for the work left after closed `c6b1b73`. The plan/schema layer for local, SSH, RunPod, and Modal exists; this issue tracks making live workers actually run, stream status/logs, sync artifacts, and finalize manifests through the provider contract.\n\n## Scope\n\nImplement live execution against the existing `ExecutionSpec` / `ExecutionPlan` direction without putting provider-specific logic directly into Studio or Mandible.\n\nRecommended implementation order:\n\n1. Generic SSH worker runner.\n2. RunPod adapter through the same SSH worker contract.\n3. Modal adapter through the same manifest/artifact semantics.\n4. Mandible-reviewed provider actions later, after Feedbax execution surfaces are stable.\n\n## Generic SSH Runner Requirements\n\n- Bootstrap or verify a supplied host/port/key/workspace.\n- Install or verify the Feedbax worker environment with `uv`.\n- Check worker health, provider version, Python/JAX/device metadata, and available capabilities.\n- Launch jobs from `ExecutionSpec` without Studio inventing a parallel execution path.\n- Stream logs/status and classify failures: allocation, SSH, environment, JAX/device, worker, graph/spec validation, training/eval/analysis failure.\n- Sync artifacts back with hashes and roles.\n- Emit/finalize manifests and artifact refs.\n\n## RunPod Requirements\n\n- Create or attach to pods using explicit provider config.\n- Poll readiness from correct RunPod fields and wait for SSH availability.\n- Execute through the generic SSH worker contract.\n- Sync artifacts and optionally stop/cleanup pods.\n- Record GPU/driver/JAX/platform metadata and provider instance metadata.\n\n## Modal Requirements\n\n- Submit generated app/function from the same execution spec shape.\n- Stream/collect logs/status.\n- Commit/sync volume outputs.\n- Emit manifests/artifact refs with provider/environment metadata.\n\n## Design Constraints\n\n- Feedbax owns execution semantics and emitted manifests.\n- Studio should call provider/execution capabilities, not embed RunPod/Modal special cases.\n- Mandible should eventually invoke reviewed provider actions; it should not implement Feedbax cloud logic.\n- Local execution remains the baseline and should share the same manifest/artifact shape.\n- Dirty dev state, package locks, environment metadata, and local overrides should be captured or explicitly warned about.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A small Feedbax job can run on a supplied SSH host using the provider execution contract and emit manifest/artifact refs.\n- RunPod execution reuses the SSH runner path rather than bespoke Studio logic.\n- Modal execution can submit, collect status/logs, and finalize artifacts/manifests for a small job.\n- Logs/status are visible through a structured provider surface and can be consumed by Studio/Mandible later.\n- Failure diagnostics distinguish infrastructure, environment, validation, and job failures.\n- Status is cross-linked back to `a3e46d5`, `c6c6da0`, `f68cf66`, and closed `c6b1b73`.\n\n## Related Issues\n\n- `a3e46d5` — product-depth and contract sequence umbrella.\n- closed `c6b1b73` — deterministic local, SSH, RunPod, and Modal execution contract plan/schema slice.\n- `c6c6da0` — provider/manifests/schema contract.\n- `f68cf66` — Feedbax as Mandible provider/plugin.\n- `e33f487` — manifest lineage and indexing.\n- `4178e12` — graph/spec worker lowering; live execution must not hide hardcoded graph assumptions.\n- `6a094c9` — Workspace runtime playback and validation overlays.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}